"throat","the throat $r = r_0$"],["line","scri","null infinity $\\mathscr{I}^\\pm$"]],"slices":[{"view":"wormhole","surface":0,"label":"$t = 0$","version":"a46373192f196760","lines":[[[-2.3265,0.0],[2.3265,0.0]]],"points":[],"fills":[],"place":{"at":[2.3265,0.0],"anchor":"tr","dx":0,"dy":1.3}}]},{"id":"bronnikov_kim","label":"Bronnikov-Kim","box":[-3.4916,3.4916,-3.3916,3.3916],"system":"bronnikov_kim","settings":"$r_0 = 1$, $Q_e = 1/2$, and $\\ell = 4\\,r_0$; $p = \\arctan((ct - x)/\\ell)$ and $q = \\arctan((ct + x)/\\ell)$, with $x$ the tortoise coordinate, zero at the throat.","caption":["The Einstein-Dirac-Maxwell wormhole ($Q_e = r_0/2$), each point in the diagram a 2-sphere of radius $r_0 + u^2$. The metric on the plane of $t$ and $u$ is $(1 - M/r)^2\\left(-c^2dt^2 + dx^2\\right)$, with the tortoise coordinate $r_*$ zero at the throat and $x = r_*\\,\\mathrm{sgn}(u)$ running over the whole line, and $p, q = \\arctan((ct \\mp x)/\\ell)$ bring it into the full diamond.","The two ends are two asymptotically flat regions, each with its own $i^0$ and $\\mathscr{I}^\\pm$, joined at the throat $u = 0$. At $Q_e = r_0$ the factor vanishes at the throat, $r_*$ runs to $-\\infty$ there, and each half of the diamond becomes the exterior of the extreme Reissner-Nordström black hole."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[3.1416,0.0],[0.0,3.1416],[-3.1416,0.0],[0.0,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[-0.0,-3.1396],[-0.0043,-3.076],[-0.0171,-3.0099],[-0.0384,-2.942],[-0.07,-2.8679],[-0.1109,-2.79],[-0.1643,-2.7026],[-0.2912,-2.5237],[-0.4455,-2.3297],[-0.6279,-2.1143],[-1.435,-1.2055],[-1.6598,-0.9469],[-1.8565,-0.7091],[-2.0013,-0.5172],[-2.0626,-0.4262],[-2.1061,-0.3545],[-2.1437,-0.2842],[-2.1688,-0.2289],[-2.1909,-0.1688],[-2.2065,-0.1111],[-2.2158,-0.0544],[-2.2187,-0.0018],[-2.2158,0.0544],[-2.2065,0.1111],[-2.1909,0.1688],[-2.1688,0.2289],[-2.1